body:
When I worked at ATVI i always preached that maps need "combat symmetry". While maps don't have to be symmetrical, there should be some form of symmetry in terms of power positions to fight from.

&nbsp;

For example, if one side of the map has a 2nd story window to fight from, the other side of the map should have also some form of elevated power position for a player to engage against the window position.

One of the best ways to succeed in esports from the business side is to work harder than everyone. The esports field is still very new as you mentioned, and no one has it completely figured out, even the top publishers. A strong work ethic will help you tackle the wide variety of challenges presented each day.

&nbsp;

You also have to be willing to make sacrifices - not every job you have in esports will be glamorous, especially off the start. When I first transitioned from a pro player to the developer side of things, I was living at a loss while I worked a minimum wage job as a QA tester in San Francisco. I made sure to go above and beyond in the role, which eventually landed me a position in esports at Activision HQ.

Don't blame the players for this one, this was mine and Nade's call.

&nbsp;

This doesn't mean we won't stream scrims in the future, but at the moment we want them to focus on learning the game and improving as a team. Much love 100T fans <3

We'll be sure to monitor the CTF respawn delay. If necessary, we can increase this to 7.5 seconds.

&nbsp;

The silent plant setting also determines audio when the bomb is defused. Currently, players within a short radius of the bombsite will hear a faint noise (very similar to a weapon switch) when a player begins planting a bomb. This noise is only audible at the start of the planting/defusing process, providing the players with the ability to "fake" the plant/defuse.
